  "body": "# Seven-source singleton universal path: `f(7) >= 20` (no new kappa)\r\n\r\nContributor: **Aaron Wang**, with help from opencode (substantial AI assistance in scoping, implementation, verification and writing; no independent human review claimed). No kappa, supplier, certificate or selected-frontier change.\r\n\r\n## Change and mathematical scope\r\n\r\nIn the [PR 943](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/943) prefix-walk model ([https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/943](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/943), `research/universal-connector-boundary`), a restored source word `w` over `n` singleton labels is universal when paired readouts realize every mask, `D(w) = {q_s xor q_t} = F2^n`; `f(n)` is the minimum universal word length. The pinned record ([https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1185](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1185), `research/universal-connector-six-source`) leaves `18 <= f(7) <= 24` with `f(7)` explicitly open. This package removes 18:\r\n\r\n> **No universal seven-source word of length 18 exists. Hence `f(7) >= 20` and the gap is `20 <= f(7) <= 24`.**\r\n\r\nThe alphabet is singletons only. The charged DUO pair-source family ([https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2396](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2396), [https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2128](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2128), [https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2156](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2156)) and the 63-mask weight-1/2/3 sparse family ([https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2229](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2229), [https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2236](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2236), [https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2397](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2397)) are distinct scopes and are recorded as concurrent, not overlapping.\r\n\r\n## Method\r\n\r\nSmallest falsifying instance first: the engine rebuilds the pinned `research/universal-connector-six-source/EXPECTED.json` byte-for-byte (945 words max 31/32; 10,395 words max 49/64; 945,945 words max 59/64; records SHA-256 `3dcc5689\u2026`, `491b295f\u2026`, `3d711ffa\u2026`), plus the counting lower bounds 10/14/18 and the Gray constructions. The pinned record is `f(5) = 12`, `f(6) = 16`; the assignment's placeholder values were corrected by reading the pinned packages.\r\n\r\nThen the length-18 census at `n = 7`, via the prefix vertex set `P = E union O` (even/odd weight):\r\n\r\n1. Position parity gives `|E|, |O| <= 9`; counting gives `|E||O| >= 64`, `C(|E|,2) + C(|O|,2) >= 63`.\r\n2. A pair-representation identity (machine-checked rows in `CERTIFICATE.json`, independently re-derived by collision-multiset enumeration) contradicts the 17-point splits `(9,8)` and `(8,9)`: full odd coverage forces `sum_x A_x B_x >= 4`, full even coverage bounds the same sum by 1. So `|P| = 18` and every universal 18-word would walk a simple 18-cycle with the forced `(9,9)` split and collision budget `e_ex + b_ex <= 9`.\r\n3. `engine.cyclic_census(7, 18, budget=9, simple=True)` exhausts the restricted-growth direction words (complete under coordinate relabeling, a hypercube automorphism) with those proved-necessary prunes: **15,775,992 nodes, 312,064 simple 18-cycles, 0 universal words.** Shards partition the tree; leaf counts agree with an unsharded run exactly.\r\n\r\nControls and non-vacuity: the cyclic census's leaf set equals the reference canonical word set exactly at `n = 5` length 10 and `n = 6` length 12; zero universal words at `n = 5` length 10 and `n = 6` length 14 reproduces `f(5) = 12`, `f(6) = 16` from the other side; planted hits are found at `n = 5` length 12 and `n = 6` length 16 and re-checked; the set-level engine agrees with a brute-force census of all 20,160,075 ten-point sets of `F2^5` (99,200 covers, none cycle-realisable) and reproduces the community nine-point result (7,888,725 sets, max 29, zero covers, [https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1166#discussioncomment-18931315](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1166#discussioncomment-18931315)). `independent.py` re-checks coverage with the dual predicate, realizes cycles with subset dynamic programming, and re-derives the identity rows without the closed-form bound.\r\n\r\n## Reproduction and checks\r\n\r\nFrom the repository root:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\npython3 -I -B research/universal-f7-singleton-seedb859517b/verify.py\r\npython3 -I -B research/universal-f7-singleton-seedb859517b/independent.py\r\npython3 -I -B research/universal-f7-singleton-seedb859517b/test_engine.py\r\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/universal-f7-singleton-seedb859517b --check-only\r\n```\r\n\r\nObserved markers:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPASS_F7_SINGLETON_GAP_VERIFY f(7) >= 20 (length 18 excluded) cycles=312064 universal_words=0 nodes=15775992 seconds=72.2\r\nPASS_F7_INDEPENDENT {\"control_sets\": \"ok\", \"lemma_rows\": {...}, \"witnesses_replayed\": 0}\r\nRan 22 tests in 154.694s \u2014 OK\r\nPASS_PACKAGE_METADATA_AND_PINS (not a mathematical acceptance check)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe decisive census is `search.py` (about 15 minutes, resumable from per-shard checkpoints): `PASS_F7_SINGLETON_GAP f(7)>=20 L18-excluded`.\r\n\r\n## Scope and open questions\r\n\r\nA finite exclusion inside [PR 943](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/943)'s abstract interface; no instantiation in the selected supplier and no kappa claim. Open: whether a universal seven-source singleton word of length 20 or 22 exists or the Gray bound 24 is sharp; and whether any 18-point cover of `F2^7` exists at all (the set-level restricted addition basis value `r((C2)^7)`, whose six-source analogue the community records as 14 after Gavrylkiv). Structured next questions are in `TASK.json` and the package README.\r\n",
